---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { icons } from '../components/icons';
import { copy } from '../content/copy';

const { contactEmail, effective } = copy.privacy;
---

<Base title="Privacy policy" description="How CoWork collects, uses, stores and deletes your information, including data from Google." indexable>
  <main class="legal" id="main">
    <a class="wordmark" href="/">
      <svg class="knot" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" set:html={icons.knot} />
      {copy.appName}
    </a>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="faint">Effective {effective}</p>

    <p>
      {copy.appName} is a private, invite-only app for couples to share projects, todos and habits. It is run by an individual, not a company, at
      <a href="https://cowork.arnavg.me">cowork.arnavg.me</a>. This policy explains what information {copy.appName} handles, why, and how you can remove it.
    </p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We only use your information to run {copy.appName} for you and the partner you pair with.</li>
      <li>We don't sell it, show ads, use analytics or tracking, or share it with anyone else.</li>
      <li>Google Calendar access is optional, and it only covers a separate “CoWork” calendar the app creates. We can't see your other calendars.</li>
      <li>You can export your data, disconnect Google Calendar, or ask for your account to be deleted at any time.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Information from Google</h2>
    <p>You sign in with Google. Depending on what you allow, {copy.appName} requests these permissions:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Sign-in (<code>openid</code>, <code>email</code>, <code>profile</code>):</strong> your Google account ID, email address, whether it's verified,
        your name and your profile picture link. We use them to check you've been invited, create your account, and show your name and picture to you and your
        partner.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Google Calendar, optional (<code>calendar.app.created</code>):</strong> lets {copy.appName} create its own “CoWork” calendar in your Google
        account and add, change and remove events in that calendar only. Todos with a due time appear there. This permission can't read, change or delete any other
        calendar or event. To keep the sync running, we store a Google refresh token, encrypted with AES-256-GCM. It is never sent to your browser.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>How we use Google user data</h3>
    <p>
      {copy.appName}'s use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
      <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" rel="noopener">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use
      requirements. In particular:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Google user data is used only to sign you in and to keep your CoWork calendar in sync. It isn't used for anything else.</li>
      <li>It is never sold, and never used or transferred for advertising, credit checks, or to build user profiles.</li>
      <li>It is never used to develop, improve or train generalized AI or machine-learning models.</li>
      <li>
        Nobody reads it, except where you ask us to (for example, to help with a problem), where it's needed for security (such as investigating abuse), or where
        the law requires it.
      </li>
      <li>It is only transferred to the service providers listed below, and only as needed to run {copy.appName}.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Information you add</h2>
    <p>
      {copy.appName} stores what you put into it: todos, notes, projects, checklists, habits and goals, completions, comments and reactions, photos you attach,
      templates, time-tracking entries, suggestions to your partner, pause dates, your time zone and notification settings. If you turn on notifications, we store
      the push subscription your browser gives us.
    </p>

    <h2>Who can see it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>You.</strong> Everything you add.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your partner,</strong> once you both choose to pair. They can see your lists, progress and photos, except anything you mark private (private todos
        and private projects, including their photos and time). Shared todos and projects can be seen and edited by both of you.
      </li>
      <li><strong>The admin,</strong> who sends invites, sees who has been invited and who has joined. The app gives the admin no view of your lists.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Service providers</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts the app and stores its database and photos (Workers, D1 and R2).</li>
      <li><strong>Google</strong> provides sign-in and, if you connect it, Google Calendar.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your browser's push service</strong> (for example Google, Apple or Mozilla) delivers notifications. Their content is end-to-end encrypted, so the push
        service can't read it.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
    <p>
      We use a session cookie to keep you signed in, and a short-lived cookie during sign-in to protect it. Your browser remembers your light/dark theme choice
      locally. There are no advertising or analytics cookies.
    </p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      Everything travels over HTTPS. Session tokens are stored only as keyed hashes, calendar tokens are encrypted at rest, and photos are kept in private storage
      and served only to people allowed to see them.
    </p>

    <h2>Keeping and deleting your data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We keep your data while your account is active. Sessions expire after 30 days without use.</li>
      <li>Deleting a todo deletes its history and photos.</li>
      <li>You can download a copy of your data (JSON or CSV) from Settings at any time.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Disconnecting Google Calendar</strong> in Settings deletes the CoWork calendar, revokes our access at Google, and deletes the stored token. You can also
        remove access from your <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" rel="noopener">Google account permissions</a> page.
      </li>
      <li>
        To <strong>delete your account</strong> and everything in it, email <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>. We'll do it within 30 days and
        confirm when it's done.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>{copy.appName} isn't meant for anyone under 13, and we don't knowingly collect their information.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, we'll update the date at the top. If a change affects how Google data is used, we'll ask for your consent again first.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions or requests: <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.</p>

    <p class="mt-4"><a class="btn ghost" href="/">Back to {copy.appName}</a></p>
  </main>
</Base>
